# data/ holds generated datasets, not authored code.
#
# linguist-generated stops GitHub counting 2,542 rows of statistics toward the
# repo's language breakdown and collapses them in pull request diffs.
#
# -diff stops git itself trying to produce a line-by-line diff of them. A
# regenerated dataset is a 2,500-line change that nobody reads and that buries
# the real diff underneath it; "binary file changed" is the honest summary.
data/* linguist-generated=true -diff
